course: dictionary
lesson: 16027
title: Ventilated: fresh air moving through
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ventilated comes from the verb «ventilate», which means to let fresh air move into a place. When a room is ventilated, fresh air can get in and stale air can get out. «The room was ventilated by an open window.» The window lets air move through, so the room is ventilated.
explain: Look at the prefix «well-» and «poorly-». «The bathroom is well ventilated, so the steam clears quickly.» Well-ventilated means there is plenty of fresh air. «The cupboard was poorly ventilated and smelled stale.» Poorly-ventilated means there is not enough fresh air.
explain: Ventilated can also describe a box or tank. «The hamster's box has holes in the lid, so it is a ventilated box.» The holes let air in, so the animal can breathe. Ask yourself: is there air moving through this? If yes, the word ventilated probably fits.
fact: Ventilated means having fresh air moving through it.
fact: Ventilate is the verb: to let fresh air move into a space.
fact: «Well-ventilated» means a room or space has plenty of fresh air.
fact: «Poorly ventilated» means a room or space does not have enough fresh air.
fact: Rooms should be well ventilated when you use paint, glue or cleaning products, so harmful fumes can leave.
exercise: «We painted the shed with the door open, because the room must be well ventilated.» What does well ventilated mean? | Is painted bright blue | Has no windows at all | *Has plenty of fresh air | Is very cold and damp
exercise: «The hamster's box has holes in its lid, so it is a ventilated box.» Why do pet boxes need holes? | So the box is lighter to carry | So the animal can see the sky | *So the animal can breathe | So the box looks pretty
exercise: «The kitchen was poorly ventilated, so the smoke stayed in the air.» Which word tells you there was not much fresh air? | smoke | kitchen | *poorly | ventilated
test: «Gas heaters must be used in a well-ventilated room.» What does this sentence tell you? | The heater must be painted | *Fresh air must be able to move in and out of the room | The room must be very small | The room must have no air at all
test: Ella says, «The tank is ventilated, so the fish are safe.» What does ventilated suggest? | The tank is full of sand | The tank is very heavy | *Air can move through the tank so the fish can breathe | Fish like to swim in the dark
exam: «The cooks lit the gas stove in a poorly ventilated kitchen.» Which choice best describes the kitchen? | *It does not have enough fresh air | It has been painted and cleaned | It is ventilated by a fan that never stops | It has plenty of fresh air and open windows
